# The jev lane is an ALLOWLIST repo.
#
# The root holds ~20 vendored clones of other people's repositories, and the set grows every
# session. An opt-out list would go stale the moment a sibling pane clones the next one, and a
# nested git repo added to this tree becomes a gitlink that nobody configured as a submodule.
# So: ignore everything at the root, then un-ignore exactly what we author.
#
# Adding a new clone requires NO change here. Adding a new first-party directory does.

/*
!/.gitignore
!/AGENTS.md
!/README.md
!/VERDICT.md
!/RECIPES.md
!/.omp/
!/LICENSE
!/visual/
!/demos/
!/EVAL.md
!/NEGATIVE_EVIDENCE.md
!/GATES.md
!/REVIEW-PERSONAS.md
!/TESTS.md
!/.fh-agents.toml
!/githooks/
!/scripts/
!/probes/
!/foundation/
# Per-machine gate run history. Append-only and written on every gates.sh run, so tracking it in a
# three-pane shared worktree would conflict constantly and tell a reader nothing they can act on.
/foundation/gate-outcomes.tsv
!/compaction/
!/ensemble/
!/work/
!/docs/
!/notes/
!/.flywheel/
!/.beads/
!/docs-mirror/
!/upstream/
# The README-NOTES sidecar is TRACKED ON PURPOSE (skill://readme-update). An untracked note is
# unreproducible: a fresh clone cannot see it, so an undrained fact would be invisible to the next
# agent exactly when it matters. Its job is to be a log that gets emptied into README.md as state.
!/README-NOTES.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docs-mirror/ and upstream/: PROVENANCE is committed, BYTES are not.
#
# `scripts/sync-docs.sh` re-fetches the mirror and `--check` proves byte identity against the
# committed sha256 manifest. So the manifests are the reviewable artifact; the 5 MB of TypeSafe
# documentation and the nested first-party clones are reproducible, third-party, and would churn
# every diff. A fresh clone runs one command to materialize them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs-mirror/*
!docs-mirror/MANIFEST.tsv
upstream/*
!upstream/MANIFEST.tsv
!upstream/ORG-INVENTORY.tsv
!upstream/UNRESOLVABLE.tsv

# Harness and tool state that belongs to a machine, never to the repo.
.ntm/
.beads/dag-graph-*.txt
.DS_Store
*.log

# Language caches and build output, wherever they appear under a first-party path.
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
.test-dist/
jev-benchmark/
awesome-typesafe/

# jevcache writes plaintext state previews to its ledger; never commit them
.jevcache-ledger/

# Harvested real shell traffic. Regenerate with:
#   node work/toolcall-judge-v3/harvest-allowed.mjs
# 77,767 real commands from our own sessions; a secret-shape scan found 66
# credential-shaped spans (bearer tokens, ghp_, AKIA, PRIVATE KEY, assignments).
# Most are our own synthetic probes, but we cannot vouch for all 77,767, and the
# file is deterministically regenerable, so it never enters git.
work/toolcall-judge-v3/real-allowed.json
